  { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Did Qwen3.8-Max open weights actually release?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Yes. Qwen3.8-Max, Alibaba\'s 2.4-trillion-parameter open-weight flagship, launched in early August 2026 and its open weights were expected to drop around August 10, 2026. Coverage from Forkast, Martin Cid Magazine and LinkedIn\'s Qwen3.8-Max "Goes Open Weight" posts all point to the August 10 release window.' } },
  { '@type': 'Question', name: 'What is Alibaba\'s revenue-share licensing plan for open weights?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Per Reuters and Forkast, Alibaba intends to charge major commercial users who self-host its open-weight models a revenue share, rather than giving the weights away as a loss leader for cloud consumption. The specific rate was still being finalized as of August 8, 2026, but the intent is to mirror Moonshot\'s Kimi K3 framework, which requires companies above roughly $20 million in annual sales to sign a commercial agreement with revenue-share rates up to 30%.' } },
